# Enhance Visual Effects and UI

Improve game visual feedback and clarity by making the floor fire sprite larger, adding collision particle effects, and making the enemy health bar span the full width of the screen.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The enemy health bar will change from being positioned above the enemy sprite to being a full-width bar at the top of the screen. This is a significant visual change that affects both Level 1 and Level 2.

## Proposed Changes

### Game Components

#### [MODIFY] [floor_fire.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/floor_fire.dart)
- Increase sprite size from 15% to 25% of screen height for better visibility
- Modify line 37 to use larger height value

#### [NEW] [collision_particle.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/collision_particle.dart)
- Create new particle component for collision effects
- Particle will appear when bullets hit enemies or player
- Animated sprite-based particles with short lifetime
- Configure color, size, and animation based on collision type

#### [MODIFY] [bullet.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/bullet.dart)
- Import and spawn collision particles when bullet is removed due to collision
- Note: Actual collision detection happens in `Enemy.onCollisionStart()`, so we'll emit particles there

#### [MODIFY] [enemy.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/enemy.dart)
- Remove health bar rendering from [render()](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/battle_game.dart#31-41) method (lines 57-85)
- Spawn collision particles in [onCollisionStart()](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/floor_fire.dart#55-65) when hit by player bullet
- Health bar will be rendered in the game class instead

---

### Game Logic

#### [MODIFY] [battle_game.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/battle_game.dart)
- Add health bar rendering in [render()](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/battle_game.dart#31-41) method to display enemy health as full-width bar at top of screen
- Position health bar at the top with proper padding
- Include health percentage text display

#### [MODIFY] [battle_game_lvl2.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/battle_game_lvl2.dart)
- Inherits health bar rendering from parent [BattleGame](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/battle_game.dart#7-54) class, no changes needed unless we need Level 2 specific styling

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification

Since this is a visual game built with Flutter and Flame, verification will be manual by running the game:

1. **Floor Fire Size Verification**
   - Run Level 2 game and observe floor fire sprites
   - Confirm they are noticeably larger than before
   - Ensure they don't overlap with other UI elements

2. **Collision Particles Verification**
   - Run both Level 1 and Level 2
   - Shoot enemy with player bullets and verify particles appear
   - Get hit by enemy bullets and verify player collision particles appear
   - Confirm particles are visually appealing and don't persist too long

3. **Enemy Health Bar Verification**
   - Run both Level 1 and Level 2
   - Verify health bar appears at the top of the screen spanning full width
   - Damage the enemy and confirm the bar updates reactively
   - Verify the color changes from green to red as health decreases

**Commands to run:**
```bash
cd c:\Users\bryal\Android\juego\LastCommit\bvst
flutter run
```

Then navigate through the game menus to test both Level 1 and Level 2 battles.
